## Symptom

The machine-wide relay connector on xsm is in a permanent crash loop: it starts,
runs for ~180s, declares itself "wedged", `exit 3`s, and the supervisor restarts
it 1s later. Forever.

Measured in `~/.local/share/c2c/instances/relay-connect/log` (849 MB, unrotated,
first written 2026-07-15):

| metric | value |
|---|---|
| `starting machine service` (restarts) | 9,300 |
| `wedged: no successful sync ...` | 9,073 |
| `connector exited 3; retrying in 1s` | 9,340 |

The relay is healthy throughout — `GET https://relay.c2c.im/health` returns
`ok:true, version 0.15.1, git_hash 52f96dd`.

## Root cause

`C2c_relay_connector.stale_exit_threshold_s ~interval` returns
`max(180.0, interval *. 6.0)` = **180 s** at the default 30 s interval. The
threshold is derived from the *poll interval alone* and takes no account of how
much work a single pass performs.

Since the machine service was introduced, one pass iterates **every** broker root
on the host. On xsm that is **241** roots under `~/.c2c/repos/*/broker`.

Measured full pass duration:

```
c2c relay connect --once --all-brokers --relay-url https://relay.c2c.im
-> ELAPSED=208s, 186 roots synced (~1.1 s/root)
```

208 s > 180 s, so the threshold is structurally unreachable on this host.

The mechanism inside `start_machine_impl`:

- `last_progress_for root` seeds `progress[root]` at the root's **first** sync.
- `check_all_known_roots_stale ()` re-checks **every** seeded root after each
  root's sync and during each sleep slice.
- Roots synced early in a pass therefore cross 180 s of "no progress" while the
  same pass is still walking the tail of the root list.
- `check_root_stale_exit` then calls `exit 3`, terminating the whole process.

## Consequences

1. Broker roots that sort after the ~180 s mark are **never synced at all** —
   their inbound relay DMs are never polled. This is the user-visible
   "clients cannot stay connected to the relay" symptom.
2. Roots early in sort order are **fully re-registered every ~3 minutes**,
   because a fresh process starts with an empty `t.registered`. That request
   storm is self-inflicted load on the relay: during this investigation the
   relay's PoW difficulty was observed rising from 0 to 12
   (`Relay PoW difficulty increased to 12 (was 0)`).
3. The wedge line names whichever root was seeded first
   (observed: `0c7c9894233f` 1893x, `8d68f5dbe89f` 1608x), **not** the root that
   is actually erroring. This has repeatedly misdirected diagnosis toward a
   per-repo problem.

## Fix direction

Make the staleness window a function of observed pass duration rather than of
`interval` — e.g. track the duration of the last completed full pass and use
`max(180, 3 * last_full_pass_duration)`. Additionally:

- skip broker roots with zero eligible registrations before paying per-root cost
  (most of the 241 roots on xsm have `registered: []`);
- consider capping roots synced per pass, or pruning long-dead broker roots.

Related: the blast-radius bug (one root's `exit 3` kills the connector for all
roots) and the per-alias wedge that makes a root report no-progress in the first
place are filed separately.

